1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,330
A little party for our team.

2
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:08,130
Decorations, cake, six happy people. I have a
perfect plan.

3
00:00:08,380 --> 00:00:10,350
Leave room for surprises.

4
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:18,760
Six plates. One for each of us.

5
00:00:19,010 --> 00:00:23,130
Aunt Rose is stopping by, but she cannot stay.

6
00:00:23,380 --> 00:00:25,780
Her chair gets a vacation.

7
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:33,760
We have one strawberry. Just in case.

8
00:00:34,010 --> 00:00:36,410
A very small emergency cake.

9
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:39,920
Let us wait for the real one.

10
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:48,760
A little ribbon for your family party.

11
00:00:49,010 --> 00:00:52,700
Thank you, Rose. Can you stay a moment?

12
00:00:52,950 --> 00:00:54,920
Just a moment, sister.

13
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:02,900
Mine keeps becoming a knot.

14
00:01:03,150 --> 00:01:05,980
Give the loops a little room.

15
00:01:06,230 --> 00:01:08,200
People need that too.

16
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:18,330
Today I have checked absolutely everything.

17
00:01:18,580 --> 00:01:23,130
Then you will know where to start if something
changes.

18
00:01:23,380 --> 00:01:26,210
That sounds like a useful plan.

19
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:34,620
We will save you a story about the party.

20
00:01:34,870 --> 00:01:37,700
That travels better than cake. Goodbye!

21
00:01:37,950 --> 00:01:39,920
See you soon, Rose.

22
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:48,330
A bow at the right address.

23
00:01:48,580 --> 00:01:51,840
That is an excellent place for it.

24
00:01:52,090 --> 00:01:55,780
And the bell can still do its job.

25
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:02,900
The entrance is still clear.

26
00:02:03,150 --> 00:02:05,550
The party can get in.

27
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:07,770
So can the people.

28
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:17,900
No ribbon under anyone’s feet.

29
00:02:18,150 --> 00:02:20,980
No mystery leftovers on the counter.

30
00:02:21,230 --> 00:02:24,060
Now we can enjoy the room.

31
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:33,330
Our address is fourteen Maple Lane.

32
00:02:33,580 --> 00:02:35,550
Blue door, number fourteen.

33
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:39,920
Even I cannot confuse the door with the cake.

34
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:48,330
Fourteen Maple Lane. Delivery around two.

35
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:50,550
Correct address, correct cake.

36
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:55,350
The confirmation is correct. We will check the
delivery too.

37
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:02,900
A space for the box.

38
00:03:03,150 --> 00:03:06,840
The strawberry has a very large neighbor
coming.

39
00:03:07,090 --> 00:03:09,490
They will both stay cool.

40
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:20,050
I will not check the cake until I see it.

41
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:23,990
There is room for that on the list.

42
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:26,640
And room in the fridge.

43
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:33,330
Dear cake, welcome to our table.

44
00:03:33,580 --> 00:03:35,980
It may need directions first.

45
00:03:36,230 --> 00:03:39,490
We will welcome it when it arrives.

46
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:47,470
A very punctual napkin.

47
00:03:47,720 --> 00:03:50,120
There is a delivery message.

48
00:03:50,370 --> 00:03:53,200
Let us see what it says.

49
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:02,900
It says delivered at two-oh-six.

50
00:04:03,150 --> 00:04:06,410
Then why is the cake not here?

51
00:04:06,660 --> 00:04:09,490
Let us check before we guess.

52
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:17,900
No box on the step.

53
00:04:18,150 --> 00:04:20,980
Not even a very small one.

54
00:04:21,230 --> 00:04:24,060
Good. That is one place checked.

55
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:32,900
No cake in the fridge.

56
00:04:33,150 --> 00:04:35,550
No cake beside the board.

57
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:40,780
Then we are looking for a delivery, not a
hidden dessert.

58
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:48,760
I wanted one afternoon without a mix-up.

59
00:04:49,010 --> 00:04:52,270
We can still have a good afternoon.

60
00:04:52,520 --> 00:04:55,780
First, let us find out what happened.

61
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:02,470
The order numbers match.

62
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:05,980
So the message is about our cake.

63
00:05:06,230 --> 00:05:09,490
A clue. Much better than a complaint.

64
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:17,900
Did somebody steal our party?

65
00:05:18,150 --> 00:05:23,560
We do not know that. A delivery could go to
another door.

66
00:05:23,810 --> 00:05:25,780
There is a photo.

67
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:32,470
That door is green.

68
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:34,520
Ours is blue.

69
00:05:34,770 --> 00:05:38,030
Then the box was photographed somewhere else.

70
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:48,330
No bow in the photo either.

71
00:05:48,580 --> 00:05:50,980
Our cake missed the decorations.

72
00:05:51,230 --> 00:05:55,350
The picture can help us ask a clear question.

73
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:02,470
Should I order another?

74
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:05,550
First check where this one went.

75
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:09,060
One missing cake is enough to investigate.

76
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:20,480
Our order is marked delivered, but the photo
shows another door.

77
00:06:20,730 --> 00:06:22,530
Clear and polite.

78
00:06:22,780 --> 00:06:26,040
With actual facts. I like this version.

79
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:32,900
The emergency strawberry is ready.

80
00:06:33,150 --> 00:06:36,410
It is one strawberry for six people.

81
00:06:36,660 --> 00:06:40,350
Let us give the cake a chance first.

82
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:48,330
There must be several green doors.

83
00:06:48,580 --> 00:06:51,410
We need the right green door.

84
00:06:51,660 --> 00:06:55,350
And we can ask before entering anyone’s space.

85
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:02,300
A leaf-shaped knocker.

86
00:07:02,550 --> 00:07:06,240
And that little hedge. I know that hedge.

87
00:07:06,490 --> 00:07:09,320
Let us check the number too.

88
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:18,330
I cannot read that last digit.

89
00:07:18,580 --> 00:07:20,980
Then do not guess it.

90
00:07:21,230 --> 00:07:25,350
We can compare the actual number at the door.

91
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:32,900
The driver recorded number eighteen.

92
00:07:33,150 --> 00:07:35,120
Our confirmation says fourteen.

93
00:07:35,370 --> 00:07:38,630
Now we have two numbers to compare.

94
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:50,480
We can ask, did a cake for number fourteen
arrive here?

95
00:07:50,730 --> 00:07:53,990
Better than, where is our entire party?

96
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:56,040
Much better.

97
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:02,900
We will all go together.

98
00:08:03,150 --> 00:08:06,410
Just along this sidewalk. No road crossing.

99
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:09,490
And straight back if nobody answers.

100
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:18,760
Blue door behind us, green door ahead.

101
00:08:19,010 --> 00:08:21,840
We are checking the actual signs.

102
00:08:22,090 --> 00:08:24,920
The sidewalk is doing excellent work.

103
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:32,470
The same low hedge.

104
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:35,980
I recognized it without asking a statue.

105
00:08:36,230 --> 00:08:39,060
A useful improvement over the park.

106
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:47,300
Number eighteen.

107
00:08:47,550 --> 00:08:49,520
Different number, different door.

108
00:08:49,770 --> 00:08:52,600
The delivery photo matches this place.

109
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:03,330
Can we peek through the hedge?

110
00:09:03,580 --> 00:09:06,410
We can ring the bell instead.

111
00:09:06,660 --> 00:09:08,460
Much less scratchy.

112
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:18,760
This is the door in the photograph.

113
00:09:19,010 --> 00:09:20,980
One question, calmly asked.

114
00:09:21,230 --> 00:09:23,200
We are all here.

115
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:32,300
Now we wait.

116
00:09:32,550 --> 00:09:34,520
I can do that.

117
00:09:34,770 --> 00:09:37,170
You have had pancake practice.

118
00:09:45,500 --> 00:09:48,330
Maybe the cake answered the door.

119
00:09:48,580 --> 00:09:51,410
Cakes are very poor at doorbells.

120
00:09:51,660 --> 00:09:54,920
Let us give our neighbor a moment.

121
00:10:00,500 --> 00:10:05,050
If nobody is home, we will ask the bakery
again.

122
00:10:05,300 --> 00:10:08,990
Yes. We do not need to look around.

123
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:12,070
We have already found useful clues.

124
00:10:15,500 --> 00:10:17,300
Someone is coming.

125
00:10:17,550 --> 00:10:19,350
Good afternoon.

126
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:21,570
Thank you for answering.

127
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:33,330
Hello. We are from number fourteen.

128
00:10:33,580 --> 00:10:38,990
We are checking a delivery that may have
reached the wrong door.

129
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:41,040
A cake delivery.

130
00:10:45,500 --> 00:10:49,190
A white bakery box with a red seal.

131
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:52,700
The photo shows it beside this door.

132
00:10:52,950 --> 00:10:55,350
We have the order confirmation.

133
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:04,190
Did a cake for number fourteen arrive here?

134
00:11:04,440 --> 00:11:08,560
We think there may have been a number mix-up.

135
00:11:08,810 --> 00:11:10,610
No hurry.

136
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:17,900
That sounds like a fridge.

137
00:11:18,150 --> 00:11:21,410
Let us hear what our neighbor says.

138
00:11:21,660 --> 00:11:24,490
Yes. We still need to check.

139
00:11:30,500 --> 00:11:33,330
Same order number, same white box.

140
00:11:33,580 --> 00:11:35,980
That will help identify it.

141
00:11:36,230 --> 00:11:38,630
And explain the mistake clearly.

142
00:11:45,500 --> 00:11:49,190
Thank you for helping us sort this out.

143
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:52,270
Our plates are waiting very patiently.

144
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:54,320
So are we.

145
00:12:00,500 --> 00:12:04,620
My perfect plan did not include asking for
help.

146
00:12:04,870 --> 00:12:08,130
There is still time to add that.

147
00:12:08,380 --> 00:12:12,070
It is a useful line on any list.

148
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:17,300
A white box.

149
00:12:17,550 --> 00:12:19,520
With a red seal.

150
00:12:19,770 --> 00:12:23,890
Let us check it before we carry it home.

151
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:32,900
That is our order number.

152
00:12:33,150 --> 00:12:35,120
And our cake description.

153
00:12:35,370 --> 00:12:38,630
Now we can ask about the label.

154
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:47,900
The order ends in ten-C.

155
00:12:48,150 --> 00:12:50,120
So does the sticker.

156
00:12:50,370 --> 00:12:55,780
The plain round cake. We have checked more
than the box color.

157
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:05,480
This came to eighteen. I put it straight in
the fridge.

158
00:13:05,730 --> 00:13:08,560
Thank you for keeping it cool.

159
00:13:08,810 --> 00:13:10,610
We appreciate that.

160
00:13:15,500 --> 00:13:19,190
The label looked like eighteen to the driver.

161
00:13:19,440 --> 00:13:21,410
Our confirmation says fourteen.

162
00:13:21,660 --> 00:13:26,210
A small mark sent a large cake on a visit.

163
00:13:30,500 --> 00:13:32,900
I have not opened it.

164
00:13:33,150 --> 00:13:35,120
The seal is intact.

165
00:13:35,370 --> 00:13:39,060
Thank you. We will take it straight home.

166
00:13:45,500 --> 00:13:48,330
Here you are. Enjoy your party.

167
00:13:48,580 --> 00:13:52,270
Thank you for being a very good neighbor.

168
00:13:52,520 --> 00:13:55,780
Our cake has had quite a trip.

169
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:02,300
Thank you again.

170
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:06,670
We will tell the bakery it is safely
recovered.

171
00:14:06,920 --> 00:14:10,610
And we will check every digit next time.

172
00:14:15,500 --> 00:14:18,330
Does it need a ticket home?

173
00:14:18,580 --> 00:14:21,410
Just a steady pair of hands.

174
00:14:21,660 --> 00:14:24,490
I have checked both of mine.

175
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:32,470
Blue door, number fourteen.

176
00:14:32,720 --> 00:14:35,120
At last, the correct entrance.

177
00:14:35,370 --> 00:14:37,770
Straight to the fridge first.

178
00:14:45,500 --> 00:14:48,760
A safe place while we get ready.

179
00:14:49,010 --> 00:14:52,270
The party can wait two more minutes.

180
00:14:52,520 --> 00:14:55,350
We have found something worth celebrating.

181
00:15:00,500 --> 00:15:04,620
Recovered safely from number eighteen. Please
check the label.

182
00:15:04,870 --> 00:15:07,270
Fourteen is still our address.

183
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:10,350
And thank you for the help.

184
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:17,900
Clean hands before we serve.

185
00:15:18,150 --> 00:15:21,410
The cake traveled farther than we did.

186
00:15:21,660 --> 00:15:24,060
Its box did the traveling.

187
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:34,620
May I have the emergency strawberry with my
slice?

188
00:15:34,870 --> 00:15:38,130
Yes. It can retire from emergency duty.

189
00:15:38,380 --> 00:15:41,210
One berry, one very important job.

190
00:15:45,500 --> 00:15:48,330
Here is our guest of honor.

191
00:15:48,580 --> 00:15:50,550
Same order, right house.

192
00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:54,490
And still cool. We can serve it now.

193
00:16:00,500 --> 00:16:02,900
The box is finally empty.

194
00:16:03,150 --> 00:16:06,840
The cake has a much better view now.

195
00:16:07,090 --> 00:16:09,490
And space for six servings.

196
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:17,300
Six equal slices.

197
00:16:17,550 --> 00:16:19,520
No four-or-forty problem today.

198
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:22,600
Just six people sharing one cake.

199
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:33,330
One for Dan, one for Leo.

200
00:16:33,580 --> 00:16:35,550
A very successful delivery.

201
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:38,630
This time we saw it arrive.

202
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:47,900
Two left on the board.

203
00:16:48,150 --> 00:16:50,980
One for Nina, one for Max.

204
00:16:51,230 --> 00:16:54,060
Exactly. No one has to guess.

205
00:17:00,500 --> 00:17:02,900
My slice has an assistant.

206
00:17:03,150 --> 00:17:04,950
The emergency strawberry.

207
00:17:05,200 --> 00:17:07,600
Six slices. Everyone has one.

208
00:17:15,500 --> 00:17:20,480
The cake is with the family. The sharp tools
stay here.

209
00:17:20,730 --> 00:17:23,560
That is a good final check.

210
00:17:30,500 --> 00:17:32,900
I wanted a perfect party.

211
00:17:33,150 --> 00:17:36,410
You made room for a real one.

212
00:17:36,660 --> 00:17:39,060
We found the cake together.

213
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:47,900
To this very helpful team.

214
00:17:48,150 --> 00:17:50,120
And our kind neighbor.

215
00:17:50,370 --> 00:17:52,770
And checking the whole address.

216
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:03,330
Did the family party start yet?

217
00:18:03,580 --> 00:18:07,270
Almost, Dad. Our cake visited the neighbor
first.

218
00:18:07,520 --> 00:18:10,350
It came back with a story.

219
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:19,620
A clear address is better than a lucky guess.

220
00:18:19,870 --> 00:18:23,130
We have been collecting evidence for that.

221
00:18:23,380 --> 00:18:25,350
Thanks, Dad. Talk soon.

222
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:32,300
Sweet. Not sour.

223
00:18:32,550 --> 00:18:34,950
And no flowers in it.

224
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:37,600
Just a very welcome cake.

225
00:18:45,500 --> 00:18:48,760
The ribbons were not the best part.

226
00:18:49,010 --> 00:18:50,810
What was?

227
00:18:51,060 --> 00:18:54,750
Everyone staying with the problem. And with
me.

228
00:19:00,500 --> 00:19:03,760
You do not have to guess alone.

229
00:19:04,010 --> 00:19:06,840
Even when your checklist looks impressive.

230
00:19:07,090 --> 00:19:08,890
Especially then.

231
00:19:15,500 --> 00:19:18,760
Emergency strawberry, thank you for your
service.

232
00:19:19,010 --> 00:19:20,980
A very small hero.

233
00:19:21,230 --> 00:19:23,030
With excellent timing.

234
00:19:30,500 --> 00:19:35,050
Would anyone like to stay right here for a
while?

235
00:19:35,300 --> 00:19:37,100
Yes.

236
00:19:37,350 --> 00:19:39,150
No directions required.

237
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:48,330
The party found the right house.

238
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:51,840
It had the right people all along.
